---
// Was jaan.li/american-community-survey/income.
import Viz from "../../../layouts/Viz.astro";
import VizEmbed from "../../../components/VizEmbed.astro";
---

<Viz
  title="Two decades of American incomes"
  description="How much 38 million people reported earning in the 2000–2022 American Community Surveys, by sector of employment, scrubbed year by year."
  eyebrow="American Community Survey"
  eyebrowHref="/visualizations/american-community-survey"
>
  <h2 class="viz-h2">The sectors where people earn most have shifted over two decades</h2>
  <p class="viz-note">
    Drag the year. The x-axis and the sector colours are pinned across every year, so what moves is
    the distribution itself rather than the frame around it. Sectors are ranked by mean income in
    2022 and that ranking is held fixed — otherwise the chart would recolour under your hand and the
    shift would be impossible to see.
  </p>

  <VizEmbed module="acs-income" export="IncomeBySectorHistorical" minHeight={560} />

  <Fragment slot="sources">
    <ul>
      <li>
        Data: <a href="https://www.census.gov/programs-surveys/acs/data.html" rel="noopener"
          >American Community Survey</a
        >, U.S. Census Bureau, 2000–2022 public use microdata samples, inflation-adjusted.
      </li>
      <li>
        Transform: <a
          href="https://github.com/jaanli/exploring_american_community_survey_data/blob/main/american_community_survey/models/public_use_microdata_sample/figures/income-histogram-with-sector-historical-inflation-adjusted-industry-mapped.sql"
          rel="noopener"
          >income-histogram-with-sector-historical-inflation-adjusted-industry-mapped.sql</a
        >.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </Fragment>
</Viz>
